            <ArticleTitle>Splenosis of the mesoappendix: case report and review of the literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>200-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The development of splenosis is a known consequence of splenic rupture. A case is presented of acute appendicitis in a patient with a past history of abdominal trauma who required laparotomy for unknown reasons. During appendicectomy a mass was found in the mesoappendix which proved to be evidence of splenosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
